The answer is yes. The complete text of the“Verses” is as follows:

“Verses” by Edgar Allan Poe

“Thy soul shall find no calm, no rest, no throne:
Beats, beats, beats, the heart of thee, the heart of me,
The heart of us, the heart of all mankind.
Sweet is the lore which binds us to our kind,
Sweet is the love which through the world hath flown,
Sweet is the final home of us, the loved, the lost.
Sweet is the joy which only virtue owns;
Sweet is the life which virtue only knows;
Sweet is the death that life from virtue parts;
Sweet is the light which only virtue shows;
Sweet is the life which virtue only knows;
Sweet is the death that life from virtue parts;
Sweet is the peace which only Virtue knows;
Sweet is the love which through the world hath flown;
Sweet is the final home of us, the loved, the lost.”

